diagnosis_text:
The reported fault — leaf_router_0_1's two uplinks simultaneously down, isolating the rack containing pc_0_1 — is not present in the live network. Every diagnostic layer was examined and returned clean results.

**Affected component:** None. All subsystems are operating normally.

**Mechanism:** The BGP snapshot shows leaf_router_0_1 (ASN 65201) has exactly 2 BGP neighbors, both in the Established state, confirming its uplinks to spine_router_0_0 (eth0) and spine_router_0_1 (eth1) are fully functional. The L2 snapshot independently confirmed that no interface on any of the 7 devices is DOWN or missing. The topology-wide reachability test recorded 0% packet loss in both directions between pc_0_0 (10.0.0.2) and pc_0_1 (10.0.1.2), with sub-millisecond round-trip times, proving end-to-end data-plane connectivity is intact.

**Localization:** No device or interface is implicated. The full Clos fabric — both leaf routers, both spine routers, and the super-spine — have all BGP sessions Established and all interfaces UP.

**Root cause:** There is no fault; the network is fully healthy and the helpdesk report does not reflect the current state of the lab.

**Fix:** No corrective action is required. The ticket should be closed as a false alarm — the connectivity between the two racks is confirmed operational at both the control plane (BGP Established) and data plane (0% loss ping) levels.
